       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided into smaller doses\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,600 mg four times daily is what you intend, please confirm that. I'd suggest adding a note with the rationale to the order."
